  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Unsettled weather is expected to return this \nweekend. \n\nA large upper level ridge and surface high pressure will remain \nacross the region through much of the work week maintaining warm and \ndry conditions. The ridge is expected to begin breaking down Friday, \nallowing moisture and northern stream shortwave troughs to reach the \nUpper Great Lakes region.\n\nA deep southerly flow is expected to move into the Ohio Valley and \nthe eastern Great Lakes region this weekend. Ensemble mean 500mb \nheights and 500 mb RH show a shortwave trough with increasing \nmoisture moving into the Ohio Valley Saturday. While confidence is \nlow on the timing and strength of the surface reflection, a period \nof showers and thunderstorms are expected with the higher \nprobability inland from the Lakes in the afternoon and evening \nhours. Ensemble Mean PWATS are forecast to be above 1.00\", which is \naround the 80th percentile for early June. Any activity could \nproduce heavy downpours. \n\nThe pattern suggests a ridge building across the Plains and Upper \nGreat Lakes and a trough across the Northeast early next week. \nEnsemble mean 500mb heights show the ridge moving eastward through \nmid-week, however some deterministic runs show an upper level low \noverhead through mid-week. Unsettled weather may continue into early \nnext week.",
